WEBVTT

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.220
"Welcome to Expo Park!"

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.180
What is this?

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.180
It's an elevator to the underground.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.810
I can see that, but... here?

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:31.600
It must be important if they went
through this much trouble to hide it.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.350
You'll see soon enough.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.470
Hmm?

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.770
Hey!

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.390
Hoodlum!

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.350
Finally caught up to you!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.970
You made it out safe!

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.310
Man, I'm so glad I asked Courier
where this place was!

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.180
Blood! Are you hurt?!

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.310
Uh...

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.770
You wouldn't believe it, lady! I totally
massacred that Executioner woman!

00:00:58.770 --> 00:00:59.140
Huh?

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.680
It was life and death! If I wasn't
so awesome, I wouldn't have lived!

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.180
I stabbed her! Right in the eye!
This blood's hers, not mine!

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.310
But look at me! Not a scratch!

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.680
--500,000,000 years, baby!
--U-Um, Hoodlum?

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.640
And the dreadlocked gorilla?

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.100
He's dead.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.850
Huh?

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:26.560
It's Brawler we're talking about!
Won't he show up half-dead again?

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.970
You're kidding, right?
Don't think you can fool--

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.930
Him and the Executioner took each other out.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.270
He's dead.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.140
No way...

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.350
If he's dead, oh well. I never
guaranteed everyone would survive.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.390
That's on him.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:47.680
Anyways, let's board the elevator.
I'd like to get there soon.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.930
What do you mean by, "Oh well"?!

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.140
Whose fault do you think
this is, you damn brat?!

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.470
You can hit me if it helps.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:02:00.560
Or stab me with a knife. Or shoot me.
We're used to that sort of thing.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.640
Maybe I'll take you up on that!

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.180
Stop! It's not going to change anything!

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.810
You okay?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.470
Keep feelings out of work.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.720
"Akudama Drive"

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.270
"The City of Lost Children"

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.180
Red! Red! Red!

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.680
Hoodlum?

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.640
I saw you drop this.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.770
Huh?

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:13.220
Sorry for losing my temper back there.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:19.020
It's fine. It's true that we used you,
and I spoke out of line.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.720
That thing is important to Brother.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:25.430
Hey!

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:28.180
If it's important, put it somewhere safe.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.140
Mind your own business.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:34.680
Sorry to spoil everyone's fun,
but how long are we riding this for?

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.600
Don't worry. We're there.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:38.720
"Arrived"

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:47.100
It's finally time for us to see
this destination of yours.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.520
I imagine if Hacker was here,
he'd be even more excited.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.720
What is this place?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:10.850
This is Expo Park. And that
right there is our destination.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.850
Hello! Bunny here!

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.140
'Sup?! It's Shark here!

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:23.180
Hey, Shark! Can you imagine what
Kansai was like before the war?

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.850
Heck no!

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:30.310
Right? That's why people before the war
wanted to preserve their culture...

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:33.890
...so that people after the war
could learn about it!

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.350
Oh! Like a museum!

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.350
You're way off the mark!

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:38.970
Huh?!

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:43.180
Apparently, they tried to
preserve a whole little city!

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.640
Wow! Kansai really spared
no expense with that one!

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:52.060
Huh? But if there's a whole city,
why haven't I seen it?!

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:56.390
Of course you haven't! It got buried
under the ground in the war!

00:05:56.390 --> 00:06:04.430
Yeah?! So if I get a shovel, I might find it?!
Then I could learn all about the past!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.310
Some things are better not to know.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.350
Well, until next time!

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.680
"The End"
"Produced by
Kansai"

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.930
This place has such weird buildings.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:25.350
I heard they were made to replicate
a festival of some sort.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.640
The past must've been whimsical.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:32.220
Oh! Courier! Look at this neat looking bike!

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:32.810
--That's no bike.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.640
--Whoa! These are some funky
clothes! Check it out, Bro!
--That's no bike.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:37.220
--Whoa! These are some funky
clothes! Check it out, Bro!
--Huh? What makes you say it's not a bike?

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:41.020
Is it 'cuz yours has tires and that one doesn't?

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.930
Why all the faded red?

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:45.350
Normally, we call that orange.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:48.600
"A world without illness"
"A Bright Future!" "Live without pain!!"
"Instant recovery from any injury!"
"The era of immortality is near!"

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.140
No matter the era, scientists
all have that same dream.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.970
We're close.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.270
So close!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.020
"Expo Park"
"Rocket Venue"

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.930
It looks a lot bigger up close!

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.640
We made it! Finally!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.520
This tower is your destination?

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:20.520
Can you at least tell us why it's so important?

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:26.430
Would you believe me if I told you that
before the war, humans went into space?

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:30.100
Space? You mean the one above the sky?

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.180
Huh?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.520
That's right.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:40.640
This tower is a vehicle that
goes to space... a rocket.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:46.390
Rocket? Space?
Where in the world are you going?

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:52.640
Before the war, humans made
a base to explore space.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.720
But there's no air, and night
and day differ by 200 degrees.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.220
It's a place where life can't survive.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:00.430
You're not...?

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.470
Yes.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.770
We're going to the Moon.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:12.270
It's the perfect place where
nobody can reach Sister and me.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.560
But why go that far?

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:19.220
We have to escape, no matter what.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:26.720
Because... we shoulder
the lives of 5,555 siblings.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:30.470
Who are you guys exactly?

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:38.310
I'll share with you our story...
About what sort of beings we are.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:52.680
Good grief. I wish they would've
made it so I don't feel pain.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:01.850
"Experiment 2502 Entering"

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:05.850
Are you all right?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:07.470
Yeah, it was fine today. Hurt though.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:10.720
"Kyushu Plant"
"Experiment Building 3 - Gymnasium"

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:10.720
Yeah, it was fine today. Hurt though.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.470
I'm glad you're okay!

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.930
I wonder why only you get experimented on...

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:19.470
Do you think they'll do the same to us someday?

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:22.140
Eww, no! It hurts, right?

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.930
It hurts quite a bit.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:29.720
But they do it to you every day.
Can't he get a break, Professor?

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.850
I don't have that authority.

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:32.850
Aww!

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:35.430
It's fine once you're used to it.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.560
Oh! You're good today!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.100
More or less.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.140
Welcome back!

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:54.520
Thanks.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.180
That was fast today!

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.640
Maybe they're used to it.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:06.890
Oh, you're done!

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:09.270
Got my head chopped twice today.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:11.600
We got you a present!

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.640
Hmm?

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.100
This!

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.770
We made it with loose threads!

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:19.140
I know it's nothing special, but...

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:21.350
No, I appreciate it!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:26.140
Just don't hang it around
your neck! You might lose it!

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.350
Good point!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.720
It'd be nice if the experiment ends soon.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.970
Professor won't help one bit! So useless!

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:41.020
I am simply an AI made to observe and teach you.
I'm not allowed to fulfill requests.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.140
Worthless!

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:45.850
Then I guess we'll just have
to ask the headmaster.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:49.140
Maybe he can stop the experiments!

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:53.680
True. If everyone here pleads with him, maybe...

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:57.470
It's all right. I'm doing just fine.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.680
And if you asked him that,
the headmaster might get mad.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:05.180
Then everyone might get tested on.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.970
You're worried about that?

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.180
We're siblings, you know!

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.350
Huh?

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:20.890
The experiment is complete.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.680
Where are they?! Where did the others go?!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.180
Experiment 2502.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.220
I've come to deliver good news today.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:53.810
Headmaster...

00:11:53.810 --> 00:12:00.640
Congratulations, Experiment 2502.
You have become the first graduate.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.180
Headmaster, where are the others?

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:07.430
At last, we've produced an
offering to send to Kanto.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:09.020
Where are the others?

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:13.600
Now we're confident in our
ability to produce graduates.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:15.310
Where are the others?!

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:20.020
But you alone aren't enough.
We will create another graduate.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:21.390
Where are the others?!

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:26.430
Rest assured. The others
will be graduating with you.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.850
This...

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.520
This can't be...!

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.930
Why are you surprised, Experiment 2502?

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:49.680
After all, you were created with 2501 children.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.680
Huh?

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.640
Professor, have you not told him?

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:57.560
I'm sorry. To preserve his
mental health, I did not.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:00.770
It's not a problem. I'll tell him now.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:03.220
We produced children with special
genes needed for immortality...

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.720
"Standby"

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.720
We produced children with special
genes needed for immortality...

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:09.180
...which were concentrated in a pool.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:14.390
From this, we produced a child
with confirmed immortality.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:19.310
In other words, you, Experiment 2502.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:23.220
From this pool, we will
produce one other graduate.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.520
Soon, we will begin mass production.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:30.350
Many more of your siblings
will join you in Kanto.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:32.720
Please look forward to it.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.520
Experiment 5557.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.600
It's your new sibling.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:03.680
Do you know what a sibling is?

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:07.680
Siblings have a stronger bond than anyone else.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.720
There's a connection that ties us together.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:14.600
We're a result of many of our siblings.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:22.020
It's fine if you don't understand.
I'm your brother and you're my sister.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:27.390
Brothers protect their sisters,
no matter what. So...

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:32.930
Come with me! I'll protect you, no matter what!

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.680
Bro... ther...

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.270
"Shinkansen"
"Carriage 1: Vault Car"

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.390
Have you forgotten anything?

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:49.020
With the backpack, we'll be fine.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.770
I will now shut down all of the systems here.

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:56.100
As planned, you two will be on your own.

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:58.060
Thank you, Professor.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:03.560
This is what they get for giving
an AI compassion. Don't mention it.

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:07.720
This is goodbye. I wish you luck.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.850
Interesting.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.180
Could be useful.

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:25.430
We stick together, no matter what.
Let's escape from this fate.

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:29.180
"Standby"

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:29.680
"Disconnected"

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:50.640
The rest of our story is as you know.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.770
I see... You're offerings to Kanto.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:59.060
To think they developed immortality.
How fascinating is that...

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:03.600
It's boring to be killed
but not die. Dying is better.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.970
I also think that's preferable.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:12.390
Are we done here? Regardless
of your situation, this job is over.

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:13.520
Yeah.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:16.970
"Kansai Credit Union"
"Deposit Confirmed"

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:19.810
"Kansai Credit Union"
"Deposit Confirmed"

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:19.810
You all did well. Thank you.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.930
Free, at last.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:32.430
Three minutes until launch.
All crew, please finish preparations.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:33.270
This is goodbye.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:38.560
Prior to launch, please ensure
to fasten your air belts.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.310
--Launching shortly. We hope you enjoy
the 12-hour journey to the Moon.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:44.600
--I hope you guys find happiness!
--Launching shortly. We hope you enjoy
the 12-hour journey to the Moon.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.140
It would be nice if we could.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:49.720
I want to eat <i>takoyaki </i>again.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:54.310
Next time we meet, you can
eat 'em till you're stuffed.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.310
Maybe... someday.

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:05.020
Keep feelings out of work.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:06.390
But...

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.720
Is it possible to keep feelings out of work?

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:23.060
Hang in there! Hang in there!

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.350
I'm fine.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.310
Huh?!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.520
I said... I'm fine.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.600
I guess you're immortal, too.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:33.310
You--!

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:35.520
Now, now. Be a good boy.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.020
What are you doing?!

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:39.850
Isn't it obvious, cutesy girl?

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:47.520
Hey, Doctor. Since you did that,
I take it you want me to kill you?

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:50.890
Must be nice to be a protected princess.

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:52.180
Huh?!

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:58.890
Took long enough... Boss.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.600
Executioners! Get in position!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.100
Wha...? Tsk!

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:08.520
Why?!

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:15.640
Boss, this is what was inside
the vault--an offering to Kanto.

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:19.850
Thanks for providing the info.
Please handle it carefully.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:23.020
What? What's the meaning of this, Doctor?!

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:27.020
I don't have to answer to you
for a single damn thing.

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:29.640
I just did what was good for me.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:33.470
To think we would join hands with an Akudama.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:39.770
I'm not letting you capture us!
We're going to the Moon!

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:42.470
Ridiculous! You can't go to the Moon!

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:45.100
We can! That's what we came here for!

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:48.310
Stupid brat! In space, you'll be dead!

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:53.430
Besides, what you think
is the Moon is an illusion!

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:57.390
It wasn't just Earth that saw the scars of war.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:59.270
You're kidding!

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.520
The flames of war even reached the Moon.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:06.770
As a result, the Moon... was destroyed!

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.220
That's enough. Playtime's over.

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.430
The offering has been recovered.

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:20.890
For attacking the <i>Shinkansen</i>
and stealing the offering to Kanto...

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:22.100
"Kansai Police"

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:22.220
"Kansai Police"

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:22.220
...you will be executed.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:23.720
"License to Kill"

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:23.720
...you will be executed.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.680
"Initializing"

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:26.970
"Launching"

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:34.020
Smoke screen!

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:35.310
You shit!

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:38.470
Where?! Where's an escape route?!

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:42.100
It's okay! It's okay! We'll find a way out--

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:45.930
Nice dodge, Swindler. It won't happen again.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.600
You guys have no business killing.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.350
Cutthroat!

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:55.470
You're the one that escaped?

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.930
We'll have your head!

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:06.850
Jeez, just give it up already!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.390
You're mine!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.100
I missed?!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.970
And here I just got my legs reattached!

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:21.600
Hmm? This is cool!

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:26.930
I kept my part of the promise.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:29.930
To think the offering was a child.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.930
Now, keep up your end of the deal.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:35.270
We're not like you Akudama.

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:39.720
As promised, we'll take you
off the Akudama list.

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:41.390
Please do.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:47.930
I...

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:54.140
I... will protect you!

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.060
--Damn brat!
--What?!

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:00.810
This way!

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:03.180
H-Hold on!

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:04.180
Get inside!

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.520
Huh? In here?!

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:07.560
--Hurry up!
--W-Wait!

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:09.850
Run! As far as you can!

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.720
--Wait!
--Brother!

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:18.060
Where did that light come from?

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:20.100
The end of the tunnel.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:25.680
--That was an act of desperation.
--What are you waiting for?! Secure the offering!

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.560
Goodbye.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.680
Offering secured!

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:54.850
Run!

00:23:44.350 --> 00:23:46.850
This is the only place I belong!
